damaged_code:
```cpp
// Thread A (Signaler)
lock.lock();
ready = true;
cond.signal(); // Signal sent before Thread B waits
lock.unlock();

// Thread B (Waiter)
// Time gap lets Thread A run first
lock.lock();
if (!ready) {
    // If ready is true, Thread B bypasses wait. 
    // BUT if Thread B has an unconditional wait:
    cond.wait(lock); // Hangs forever!
}
lock.unlock();
```

fix:
Always guard the wait with a state predicate check.
```cpp
lock.lock();
while (!ready) {
    cond.wait(lock);
}
lock.unlock();
```
